6  Other income for the quarter has increased significantly compared to the previous periods. This increase is primarily attributable to the reversal of a previously recognized loss provision of Rs 500 lakhs related to a long  term contract. The reversal was made following a current reassessment based on updated information and developments regarding the contract  which indicated that the loss previously anticipated is no longer expected to materialize . &lt;BR&gt; 
7  An exceptional item  expense of Rs 400 lakhs has been recognised in the financial results for the quarter  representing an ex  gratia compensation extended to employees affected by the accident at the Companys manufacturing facility. &lt;BR&gt; 
8  The figures for the corresponding previous period have been reclassified  regrouped wherever necessary to conform to current period classification. &lt;BR&gt; 
